  "rules": [
    "Ivory uses champagne; Ink Blue uses platinum and pale ice blue for interface actions, focus and metallic edges.",
    "External web sources retain a dashed neutral boundary.",
    "Sub-source colors stay within their parent pigment family.",
    "Arabic source excerpts use Amiri with right-to-left text direction.",
    "Use consistent sharp corners for controls and panels.",
    "Sample text and data are design specimens, not independently verified research.",
    "Ink blue is the secondary interface color; dark green is reserved for Islamic provenance.",
    "Use vibrant gold, cyan-blue, green, violet and silver-blue gradients for provenance underlines and source markers.",
    "Multiline underlines use box-decoration-break: clone; body text remains in the normal reading color."
